.docname {BakingRL SDK}
.docauthor {BakingRL}
.include {docs}
.doclang {en}

BakingRL SDK contains the TypeScript contracts, helper functions, and package
scaffolding tools used to build BakingRL plugin packages.

This site is generated as a multi-page Quarkdown documentation site. Use the
left navigation to move between sections and the right navigation for the table
of contents of the current page.

The current SDK version is `0.3.0`. Generated packages declare runtime API
`0.3.0`, and current BakingRL hosts support `>=0.3.0 <0.4.0`.

## Start Here

- [Introduction](chapters/introduction.qd): repository purpose, plugin
  capabilities, and compatibility.
- [Getting Started](chapters/getting-started.qd): local SDK install, package
  creation, and the development loop.
- [Authoring Workflows](chapters/authoring-workflows.qd): common plugin
  authoring patterns with TypeScript, services, components, and separate
  HTML/CSS files.
- [SDK API](chapters/sdk-api.qd): TypeScript helpers and runtime contexts.
- [Plugin Package Format](chapters/plugin-package-format.qd): manifest schema,
  export types, and bundle structure.
- [Package CLI](chapters/package-cli.qd): generator and package helper commands.
- [Security Model](chapters/security-model.qd): host-enforced permissions and
  package boundaries.
- [Telemetry Types](chapters/telemetry-types.qd): Rocket League event names and
  typed payloads.

## Source Of Truth

The SDK owns plugin authoring contracts, templates, helper CLI behavior, and
manifest type definitions. The host application owns runtime enforcement,
package installation, permission checks, page rendering, overlays, and OBS
gateway behavior.
